Xviewer packaging for Debian
============================

Repository layout
-----------------

The main branch is the Debian packaging branch. The upstream/latest branch
contains imported upstream releases, and the pristine-tar branch contains the
metadata required to reproduce orig tarballs.

The initial repository contains only Debian packaging. Import the upstream
source before attempting a package build.

Preparing the 3.4.16+ds upstream source
---------------------------------------

Linux Mint did not publish a semantic 3.4.16 source tag. Its master.lmde7
release points to commit 74d7d4ba2584c658ae6fb87208543671664943cc, whose
Meson project version is 3.4.16. The exact commit archive is used so that the
input cannot change if Linux Mint moves a release tag.

Run the following commands from the repository root:

    upstream_version=3.4.16
    upstream_commit=74d7d4ba2584c658ae6fb87208543671664943cc
    wget -O ../xviewer-${upstream_version}.tar.gz \
      https://github.com/linuxmint/xviewer/archive/${upstream_commit}/xviewer-${upstream_version}.tar.gz
    mk-origtargz --package xviewer --version ${upstream_version}+ds \
      --repack --compression xz ../xviewer-${upstream_version}.tar.gz
    gbp import-orig --pristine-tar --upstream-version=${upstream_version}+ds \
      ../xviewer_${upstream_version}+ds.orig.tar.xz

The Files-Excluded field in debian/copyright removes Linux Mint's debian
directory from the orig tarball. The +ds suffix records that repacking.

The watch file is ready for future semantic version tags. It cannot discover
the current master.lmde7 tag because that tag does not contain the upstream
version number. Check upstream's Meson version and releases manually until
upstream starts publishing semantic version tags.

Building and checking
---------------------

Build an unsigned source package, then rebuild that source package in a clean
Debian unstable environment:

    dpkg-buildpackage --build=source --no-sign
    sbuild -d unstable ../xviewer_3.4.16+ds-1.dsc

Inspect every Lintian result rather than overriding it:

    lintian --display-info --display-experimental --pedantic \
      ../xviewer_3.4.16+ds-1_*.changes

Run the installed-package tests against the generated binary packages:

    autopkgtest ../xviewer_3.4.16+ds-1_amd64.changes \
      -- schroot unstable-amd64-sbuild

Replace amd64 with the architecture being tested. The null testbed is also
usable on a disposable test virtual machine, but it installs packages directly
on that machine and provides less isolation than the schroot testbed.

Also install the generated packages in a fresh graphical Debian virtual
machine and manually test image opening, navigation, zoom, rotation, save,
print preview, fullscreen, slideshow, metadata, and help.

Salsa continuous integration
----------------------------

The root .gitlab-ci.yml starts Salsa CI automatically when this repository is
imported as a Salsa project. Debian's preferred long-term setup is to select
debian/salsa-ci.yml as the project's CI/CD configuration file in Salsa. Both
files include the same official Debian recipe; keep only the active entry if a
sponsor or packaging team requests that the duplicate be removed.

Before requesting sponsorship
-----------------------------

Keep the changelog distribution as UNRELEASED while developing. After clean
builds and tests, use dch --release --distribution unstable to finalize it.
Build and sign the source package with debuild -S -sa, upload the resulting
source changes file to mentors.debian.net, and file a Request for Sponsorship.

Bug #830615 is the existing Request for Package for Xviewer. Retitle it to an
Intent To Package and set yourself as its owner before requesting sponsorship.
The changelog's Closes entry will close it only after the package is accepted
into the Debian archive.
